# apps/api — NestJS 11

ESM. Relative imports use `.js` extensions.

## Module layout (common pattern)

```
feature/
  feature.module.ts
  feature.controller.ts   # routes + DTO binding only
  feature.service.ts      # authz + orchestration
  feature.repository.ts   # Prisma queries (when used)
  dto/*.dto.ts
  *.spec.ts
```

Controllers stay thin. No Prisma in controllers.

Many data-heavy features use `*.repository.ts` (~20 modules). Smaller modules (e.g. `tax-configs`, parts of `etl`) call `PrismaService` from the service — **do not add a repository layer** unless the feature already has one or complexity warrants it.

## Global stack (`app.module.ts`)

- `ConfigModule.forRoot` + `validateEnv`, `PrismaModule`, `StorageModule`, `JobsModule`.
- Filters/interceptors: `GlobalExceptionFilter`, `ResponseTransformInterceptor`, `LoggingInterceptor`.
- Guards (`APP_GUARD` order): `ThrottlerGuard` → `ClerkAuthGuard` → `PermissionsGuard` → `TenantGuard`.

## Auth decorators

```ts
@Public()
@RequirePermission(PERMISSIONS.SURVEY_VIEW)
@RequireAnyPermission(...)
@CurrentUser() user: AuthenticatedUser
```

Permissions: `common/constants/permissions.ts`. `TenantGuard` checks geo IDs when present — repositories must still apply `buildTenantWhere`.

## Prisma

```ts
constructor(private readonly prisma: PrismaService) {}
await this.prisma.db.survey.findMany(...)
import type { Prisma } from "@workspace/database"
```

Use `getSkipTake`, `toPaginatedResult`, `buildOrderBy`, `buildTenantWhere`.

## DTOs

- Global `ValidationPipe`: `whitelist`, `transform`, `forbidNonWhitelisted`.
- Query numbers: `@Type(() => Number)` + `@IsInt`.
- Lists: extend `PaginationQueryDto` or feature query DTO.

## Jobs

- Enqueue via `apps/api/src/jobs/jobs.service.ts` only — do not `@InjectQueue` in API feature modules.
- Queue/job names and payloads from `@workspace/jobs`.
- Worker processors may `@InjectQueue` for job chaining (e.g. import → image migration, ETL pipelines).

## Errors

- Throw Nest HTTP exceptions with clear messages.
- `GlobalExceptionFilter` maps Prisma `P2002` → 409.
- Never return raw Prisma errors to clients.
